  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Throw-ins from every line",
  "description": "Six against six on a pitch of about 50 × 40 metres, with a goal and a goalkeeper at one end and two small goals at the other. The team with the goalkeeper defends the big goal and attacks the two small ones; at half-time the teams swap roles. Goals are scored by rolling or side-footing the ball in from close range – mark a zone of about five metres in front of each goal with cones.\n\nExtra rule: every time the ball goes out, over any line, it is a throw-in from where it went out. That gives lots of throw-ins, and defending them is what you are practising. If you win the ball before the other team has made three passes after their throw-in, you get a bonus point.\n\nVariation: play with more players if you do in matches. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Mark on the right side – between your player and your own goal."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "See both the thrower and your player, and go with the run."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Don't forget the thrower: once the ball is thrown, they are a player like any other."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Cover the space behind the others so a long throw doesn't go straight through."
    }
  ],
